    "title": "SNL Syntax Tree",
    "content": {
      "snl": "interface(SnlSyntaxTree,enumerate(Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.macro_name,string),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.style_name,Type.opt(string)),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.env_mode,Type.opt(Type.union(Type.literal(formula_inline),Type.literal(formula_display),Type.literal(text),Type.literal(block)))),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.temporary_source,Type.opt(string)),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.temporary_format,Type.opt(Type.literal(texttt))),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.kind,string),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.scope,Type.opt(string)),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.binder_explicit,Type.opt(boolean)),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.binder_name,Type.opt(string)),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.postfix,Type.opt(SnlPostfix)),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.source,Type.opt(SnlResolvedSource)),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.mdata,unknown),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.children,Type.array(SnlSyntaxTree))))",
      "markdown": "The primary `SnlSyntaxTree` is the flat interface in `types.ts`, not the auxiliary mode-discriminated union. The parser emits ordered children and syntax metadata. Temporary literal nodes use coordinate names (`#`, `#0.1`, etc.) in `macro_name`, with the literal payload in `temporary_source` and the delimiter mode in `env_mode`. Rendering mode for a regular Macro comes from its selected complete template. `source`, `postfix`, binder flags and names are distinct fields; arbitrary `mdata` is not a replacement for them."
    },
